# From Forgotten Distinctions to Heat

A deterministic decision can collapse many inputs into one visible answer. This notebook follows that collapse from finite counting to an energy lower bound. Start with the [Landauer principle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landauer%27s_principle), then explore the state-count model directly.

{{interactive_demo:0}}

The governing quantity is $e_n=\log_2|A_n|-\log_2|f_n(A_n)|$. The first computational audit enumerates a parity decision and counts its image.

{{demo:0}}

<details><summary>Click to reveal the counting theorem and proof sketch</summary>

If $b(n)+\log_2|f_n(A_n)|\le\log_2|A_n|$, subtracting the image term gives $b(n)\le e_n$. Since $k_BT\ln2\ge0$, multiplication preserves the inequality and yields $b(n)k_BT\ln2\le e_nk_BT\ln2$.

</details>

